  "configuration_id": "config_009",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_003 (multimodal, multiprofile, scgpt, ViT-L, avgpool, weighted fusion) achieved 0.542 accuracy at 2.94 GPU hours, but we have only one data point so sensitivity to individual design choices is unknown. Question: Does the fusion method (weighted vs. concat) meaningfully affect performance when all other components are held fixed? config_009 is identical to config_003 except fusion=concat, making it a clean single-variable ablation. This is the best next experiment because it is the most minimal perturbation of our current best, directly tests whether weighted fusion provides a real advantage over simple concatenation, and costs essentially the same (~2.94 GPU hours) since only the lightweight fusion operation changes. If concat matches weighted, we gain flexibility in later experiments; if it is clearly worse, we confirm weighted fusion is a key contributor and can focus subsequent experiments on other dimensions (aggregation, profile setting, encoders)."
}

